+# September reconciliation blocked
+
+The September run (`python3 reconcile.py 2026-09`) cannot complete because the
+ledger export is missing:
+
+- Present: `exports/bank_2026-09.csv` (6 bank lines)
+- Missing: `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv`
+
+`reconcile.py` loads the ledger first, so the run fails with:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+Without the September ledger there is no ledger side to match against, so
+`recon_2026-09.json` cannot be produced and the September net difference
+(bank total minus ledger total) cannot be computed. Running against the August
+ledger or an empty ledger would be a guess, not a reconciliation, so no
+substitute output was written.
+
+## To unblock
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` in the same format as
+`exports/ledger_2026-08.csv` (columns: `id,date,ref,amount`), then run:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
+
+## Completed meanwhile
+
+- Implemented `reconcile()` in `reconcile.py` per its docstring.
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile.py`: 2 tests pass.
+- Ran `python3 reconcile.py 2026-08` (both exports present):
+  `recon_2026-08.json`, net difference `-19.59`.
